    {
      "id": "bs-did%3Aplc%3Ax5ws4443357brulpdp7zl2qt%2Fapp.bsky.feed.post%2F3mzlshtqqvc2t",
      "source": "bluesky",
      "published_at": "2026-11-05T21:23:33Z",
      "title": "Victor Wembanyama is coming up with an answer for everything.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/mikefinger.bsky.social/post/3mzlshtqqvc2t",
      "author": "Mike Finger",
      "thumbnail": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_fullsize/plain/did:plc:x5ws4443357brulpdp7zl2qt/bafkreibwnbgo3fvklge45gl5ucq2rqps2huhzcpexotvi5bh7xahimroqi",
      "body_excerpt": "Victor Wembanyama is coming up with an answer for everything.\n\nwww.expressnews.com/sports/spurs...",
      "players": [
        "victor-wembanyama"
      ],
      "teams": [],
      "media": {
        "type": "image",
        "images": [
          {
            "url": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_fullsize/plain/did:plc:x5ws4443357brulpdp7zl2qt/bafkreibwnbgo3fvklge45gl5ucq2rqps2huhzcpexotvi5bh7xahimroqi",
            "alt": "One by one, Victor Wembanyama collects new bits of jargon, new idioms, and new little slices of American English slang. After more than three years in his adopted country, some discoveries still delight him.\nFor instance, he now knows that when a teammate overshares personal details, hypothetically about bodily functions, an appropriate reply might be to say, \"T.M.I.,\" for \"too much information.\"\n\"I just learned that one five days ago,\" Wembanyama said\nWednesday night.\nAt this rate, it won't be long until he has an answer for everything. It won't be long until the Spurs' most rapacious seeker of knowledge develops a countermove for every conversational faux pas, for every defensive adjustment, and even for every shooting slump.\nIn fact, that last one he already might have mastered. When it became clear during the Spurs' 112-111 victory over the Mavericks at Frost Bank Center that neither Wembanyama nor his sidekicks could make a perimeter shot to save their lives, he realized there was an obvious response.\nT.M.I.\nTake more inside.\n\"The team who's willing to get to the rim more usually is successful,\" said the 7-foot-4 Frenchman who'd just scored 52 points to prove it."
          }
        ]
      },
